// Originally libraries defined in this file were thought to be separated into 2 libraries for
// "framework" and "services", for "classes that needs to be in the bootclasspath and jarjared" and
// "classes that don't need to be in the bootclasspath". This turned out to not work because
// different modules need different classes in their bootclasspath.

// Then smaller libraries were created for more specific functionalities: netlink structs, IP
// structs, BPF utils etc. This turned out not to work because they sometimes depended on common
// classes (for example Struct) that may or may not be in the classpath of the user:
// service-connectivity might already have it through framework-connectivity, but NetworkStack does
// not. Also it created many build rules with unclear boundaries.

// Then common dependency libraries were split out and comments were added to say "users of this
// library must ensure they have this dependency included or in their classpath". At that point
// there were too many libraries and everything is very messy.

// The current plan is to define one library per user: one for framework-connectivity
// (net-utils-framework-connectivity), one for service-connectivity
// (net-utils-service-connectivity), one for framework-wifi (net-utils-framework-wifi)...
// This is achieved by defining a *private* filegroup that lists classes that need to be in the
// bootclasspath (net-utils-framework-connectivity-srcs), using it to build
// net-utils-framework-connectivity, and building *all* the other classes in
// the service jar (net-utils-service-connectivity) by using net-utils-all-srcs as "srcs" and
// net-utils-framework-connectivity-srcs as "exclude-srcs". R8 should take care of stripping out
// unused classes in service jars.
// For APKs that do not have net-utils with matching jarjar rules in their bootclasspath like
// NetworkStack, CaptivePortalLogin, tests, they can use net-utils-connectivity-apks that just
// includes everything.
// See TODO comments on remaining items for that migration.

package {
    default_team: "trendy_team_fwk_core_networking",
    default_applicable_licenses: ["Android-Apache-2.0"],
}

